    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0385" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1121 Osborn, L. C./2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-17T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1928—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>362. My 266 April 25, 10 a.m. Osborn has telegraphed his wife from Kaifengfu that
                    he is “with Ashcraft.”<anchor n="13" xml:id="d221-f1"/> It is presumed therefore
                    that he is released and safe.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d221-f1" n="13" xml:id="d221-f1-content">
                <p>Rev. E. P. Asheraft, superintendent of the American Free Methodist Mission,
                    Jungtseh, Honan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
